<h1>About JobHunt HQ</h1>

<p class="pitch">Track every application. Prepare with your own AI. Apply as yourself.</p>

<section class="dashboard-section">
    <h2>The story</h2>
    <p>
        JobHunt HQ was built from scratch on Azure by a solo developer — partly
        as a hands-on way to learn cloud development with something real, and
        partly as an exercise in starting a small product and brand from
        nothing. It is an independent personal project, not a company with a
        sales team, and it is maintained by its builder.
    </p>
    <p>
        The idea came from the builder's own job-search workflow: his AI
        assistant helps him find postings, check them against his criteria,
        and prepare applications — while he reviews and submits every one
        himself. JobHunt HQ packages the preparation half of that workflow so
        anyone can do the same with their own AI.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="dashboard-section">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p>
        JobHunt HQ tracks your applications as a pipeline, checks each new
        posting against your own search profile — your pay floor, must-haves,
        deal-breakers, and skip list — and builds a preparation view for every
        application. Its centrepiece is the <strong>AI packet</strong>: a
        self-contained document (Markdown or JSON) holding the posting, the
        fit verdict with its reasons, your profile and standing answers, and
        your resume's text, wrapped in strict instructions for your AI
        assistant. Hand the packet to ChatGPT, Claude, or any AI you use, and
        it can help you prepare — using only your facts.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="dashboard-section">
    <h2>What it never does</h2>
    <p>
        JobHunt HQ <strong>never submits an application for you</strong>, never
        logs into a job board or an employer's site as you, and never invents
        experience or answers. Every packet instructs the AI to stop before
        any final submission. You review, you decide, you press submit — the
        way an application should work.
    </p>
    <p>
        Your data is yours: resumes live in private storage and are only ever
        served back to you, your information is not sold, and nothing you save
        here is used to train models.
    </p>
</section>
